OL,3,GNEWSASecurity patrol 'abused power',
OL,4,Acouncil told
OL,5,
OL,6,FPrivate security guards hired to patrol
OL,7,Ftowns visited by asylum seekers "abused
OL,8,Fpower" by handcuffing two female
OL,9,Fteenagers alleged to have been
OL,10,Fshoplifting, a council meeting heard.
OL,12,FThe guards had been hired by Reform
OL,13,FUK-led Essex County Council in response
OL,14,Fto what it said were residents'
OL,15,Fconcerns.
OL,17,FBut Colchester City Council heard a
OL,18,Fcomplaint of assault had been made
OL,19,Fagainst them over a city centre
OL,20,Fincident, with Labour's Tim Young
OL,21,Ftelling a meeting "power had gone to
OL,22,Ftheir heads" and they had "abused it".
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
